      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T22:04:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "gether_set_gadget() is only ever called from a drivers bind(). It was my understanding that the gadget framework protects against the removal of the gadget during framework api calls. `struct usb_gadget` doesn\u0027t have an explicit lock from what I can tell.\n\nDoing some further digging on this, I don\u0027t think we need to worry about the disconnect events as bind is called before the connection is established, but was concerned about the potential for a role switch from gadget to host mode to cause an issue.\n\nBecause this goes back to the driver core, I believe the device lock protects us from the role switch case because unbind() can\u0027t be called while bind() is active.\n\nPlease let me know if there\u0027s something I\u0027m missing",
      "parentUuid": "914d55c2_2d199e29",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 894,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 894,
        "endChar": 6
