      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T22:04:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can do that though I\u0027m still trying to figure out if the unbind logic is necessary. Is gether_update_gadget or gether_bind_gadget more appropriate here? Alternatively, I can rename this function and wrap it in gether_set_gadget() and gether_unset_gadget() to prevent having to refactor multiple gadgets.\n\nThat being said, the patch this is attempting to address (a04224da1f34) changes the f_ncm.c logic, but does not change the same pattern for other gadgets which call gether_update_gadget(), including f_ecm.c, f_eem.c, f_rndis.c, and f_subset.c. I\u0027m starting to think that an upstream revert of this patch is more appropriate while identifying a more extensive refactor of all the network gadgets to handle this properly.",
